WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.090
The future rarely unfolds exactly as expected.

00:00:03.090 --> 00:00:06.700
Structured techniques encourage analysts to explore alternative futures and identify

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:09.000
factors that could lead to different outcomes.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.120
This work often begins with key assumptions.

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:14.320
If a major assumption changes, what paths become more likely?

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:18.325
What early indicators would suggest movement toward one path instead of another?

00:00:18.325 --> 00:00:21.695
Considering multiple possibilities improves preparedness and reduces overconfidence.

00:00:21.695 --> 00:00:26.105
It helps teams plan for uncertainty instead of treating one forecast as the only plausible

00:00:26.105 --> 00:00:26.840
outcome.

00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:28.390
The objective is not precise prediction.

00:00:28.390 --> 00:00:31.180
The objective is understanding what could happen, why it could happen,

00:00:31.180 --> 00:00:33.000
and how organizations might respond.
